    "text": "<p>Let the system of linear equations<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />have a unique solution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>y</mi></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> are collinear points, then the sum of absolute values of all possible values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;is</p>"
